---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import '@fontsource/outfit/400.css';
import '@fontsource/outfit/500.css';
import '@fontsource/outfit/600.css';
import browser from '../../styles/components/browser.css?url';
import diagram from '../../styles/components/diagram.css?url';
import social from '../../styles/components/social.css?url';
import tabs from '../../styles/components/tabs.css?url';
import page from '../../styles/projects/nuru.css?url';
---

<ProjectLayout slug="nuru" styles={[browser, diagram, social, tabs, page]}>
  <div class="cover">
    <figure class="cv-img">
      <img
        src="/media/nuru/cover.webp"
        alt="The nuru homepage in a browser beside the nuru app on a phone, showing the next consultation, today’s menu and the water tracker"
      />
    </figure>
    <div class="cv-deco" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="cv-ring"></span>
      <svg class="cv-ln" viewBox="0 0 106 30">
        <polyline class="cl" points="4.3,1.2 105.4,29.5"></polyline>
      </svg>
      <span class="x cv-x1"></span>
      <span class="x cv-x2"></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="sec first" id="s-overview" data-sec aria-labelledby="h-overview">
    <div class="sh">
      <h2 class="sh-t" id="h-overview">
        Overview
      </h2>
      <span class="sh-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="x sh-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split-a">
        <p class="lead">Quick fixes are everywhere. Lasting change isn’t.</p>
        <p class="tx">
          Takeaway is one tap away, and injections or operations promise fast results. Yet many people are still unhappy
          with their body, or simply too busy for a proper meal.
        </p>
        <p class="tx">
          nuru is a case study for a service that connects people with licensed dietitians, practical meal plans and an
          app that keeps the routine going. I mapped the service first, then designed the website, the client app and
          the brand.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-b">
        <span class="vl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <dl class="facts">
          <div>
            <dt>Scope</dt>
            <dd>Website, app and brand</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Platform</dt>
            <dd>Website · iOS and Android app</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>UX maps</dt>
            <dd>Stakeholders, journey, site flow, architecture</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
    <table class="cmp rv">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">The quick fix</th>
          <th aria-hidden="true"></th>
          <th scope="col">
            <span class="mk olive" aria-hidden="true"></span>With nuru
          </th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Ordering in because there’s no time to cook</td>
          <td class="cmp-a" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="hd fr"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-r"></span>
          </td>
          <td>Meals planned around your working week</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Injections or operations that work for a while</td>
          <td class="cmp-a" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="hd fr"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-r"></span>
          </td>
          <td>Habits that keep working long after you start</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Strict diets you follow on your own</td>
          <td class="cmp-a" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="hd fr"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-r"></span>
          </td>
          <td>A dietitian who adjusts the plan with you</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Guilt after every “bad” meal</td>
          <td class="cmp-a" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="hd fr"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-r"></span>
          </td>
          <td>A calmer, more flexible relationship with food</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="s-ux" data-sec aria-labelledby="h-ux">
    <div class="sh">
      <h2 class="sh-t" id="h-ux">
        UX process
      </h2>
      <span class="sh-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="x sh-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="stack">
      <p class="lead">Mapping the service before designing a screen.</p>
      <p class="tx">
        Four maps shaped every decision: who nuru serves and depends on, how one person’s week actually feels, how a
        visitor becomes a client, and what the system needs behind it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tbw">
      <div class="tb" role="tablist" aria-label="Service maps">
        <button
          class="tb-b"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="tb-sm"
          aria-controls="tp-sm"
          aria-selected="true"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          Stakeholders
        </button>
        <button
          class="tb-b"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="tb-jr"
          aria-controls="tp-jr"
          aria-selected="false"
          tabindex="-1"
        >
          User journey
        </button>
        <button
          class="tb-b"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="tb-sf"
          aria-controls="tp-sf"
          aria-selected="false"
          tabindex="-1"
        >
          Site flow
        </button>
        <button
          class="tb-b"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          id="tb-ar"
          aria-controls="tp-ar"
          aria-selected="false"
          tabindex="-1"
        >
          System
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="tb-p" role="tabpanel" id="tp-sm" aria-labelledby="tb-sm">
        <div class="subh">
          <h3 class="h3">Clients, dietitians and the platform between them.</h3>
        </div>
        <div
          class="sm rv"
          role="group"
          aria-label="Stakeholder map: clients send needs and goals to the nuru platform and get a plan and support back; the platform sends matched clients to dietitians, who bring expertise and plans; the nuru team, care teams and families, service providers and regulators support it"
        >
          <div class="sm-cl">
            <div class="sm-hd" style="grid-column: 1 / -1">
              <span class="mk clay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <h4>Clients</h4>
              <p>Different ages, bodies and health needs, not one average dieter.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="sm-g">
              <span class="ulabel">Age</span>
              <ul class="tg">
                <li>18 to 29</li>
                <li>30 to 49</li>
                <li>50 to 64</li>
                <li>65 and over</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="sm-g">
              <span class="ulabel">Gender and life stage</span>
              <ul class="tg">
                <li>Women</li>
                <li>Men</li>
                <li>Non-binary</li>
                <li>Pregnancy</li>
                <li>Menopause</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="sm-g">
              <span class="ulabel">Health needs</span>
              <ul class="tg">
                <li>Diabetes</li>
                <li>Insulin resistance</li>
                <li>Celiac disease</li>
                <li>Eating disorders</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="sm-g">
              <span class="ulabel">Goals</span>
              <ul class="tg">
                <li>Lose or gain weight</li>
                <li>Busy working weeks</li>
                <li>A lasting routine</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sm-v" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="vd fd" style="left: calc(36% - 2px)"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-d" style="left: calc(36% - 4px); bottom: 0"></span>
            <span class="vd fu" style="left: calc(64% - 2px); top: 6px; bottom: 0"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-u" style="left: calc(64% - 4px); top: 0"></span>
            <span class="sm-vl" style="right: calc(64% + 12px)">
              needs, goals
            </span>
            <span class="sm-vl" style="left: calc(64% + 12px)">
              plan, support
            </span>
          </div>
          <span class="dm sm-dm" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="sm-pf">
            <span class="mk ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <h4>nuru platform</h4>
            <p>Website and app. Matches each client to a dietitian by age, life stage and condition.</p>
            <span class="vd sm-down" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="sm-h" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="sm-hl" style="top: 0">
              matched clients
            </span>
            <span class="hd fr" style="top: 22px; right: 6px"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-r" style="top: 20px; right: 0"></span>
            <span class="hd fl" style="top: 36px; left: 6px"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-l" style="top: 34px; left: 0"></span>
            <span class="sm-hl" style="top: 46px">
              expertise, plans
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="sm-di">
            <div class="sm-hd">
              <span class="mk olive" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <h4>Dietitians</h4>
            </div>
            <p>Licensed, and matched by speciality rather than by chance.</p>
            <span class="ulabel">Specialities</span>
            <ul class="tg col">
              <li>Weight management</li>
              <li>Eating disorder recovery</li>
              <li>Diabetes and insulin resistance</li>
              <li>Pregnancy and celiac nutrition</li>
            </ul>
            <p>They also write and review the tips and sample plans on the website.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sm-bus" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="hd"></span>
            <span class="sm-bc"></span>
            <span class="sm-bc up"></span>
            <span class="sm-bc"></span>
            <span class="sm-bc"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="sm-sup">
            <div class="sm-s">
              <span class="mk ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <h5>nuru team</h5>
              <p>
                Product, content editors and support. They need trust and a clear view of what helps clients, and bring
                the platform, matching and content.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="sm-s">
              <span class="mk out" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <h5>Care team and family</h5>
              <p>
                Doctors, therapists and caregivers. They need plans that stay in line with treatment, and bring medical
                guidance and referrals.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="sm-s">
              <span class="mk out" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <h5>Service providers</h5>
              <p>
                Payments, video calls, notifications and app stores. They need a stable integration, and bring the
                infrastructure nuru runs on.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="sm-s">
              <span class="mk out" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <h5>Regulators and associations</h5>
              <p>
                Health and data regulators, dietetic associations. They need licensed practice and protected data, and
                bring rules and credibility.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lg">
          <span>
            <span class="mk clay"></span>Clients
          </span>
          <span>
            <span class="mk olive"></span>Dietitians
          </span>
          <span>
            <span class="mk ink"></span>nuru team
          </span>
          <span>
            <span class="mk out"></span>External partners
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tb-p" role="tabpanel" hidden id="tp-jr" aria-labelledby="tb-jr">
        <div class="split">
          <div class="split-a stack" style="margin-top: 0">
            <h3 class="h3">From a late takeaway to a routine he keeps.</h3>
            <p class="tx">Six stages, what John does, thinks and feels, and what nuru should do at each one.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="split-b persona">
            <span class="vl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="ulabel">Persona</span>
            <b>John, 34, project manager</b>
            <p>Works long days and orders in most evenings. Wants to lose weight without another strict diet.</p>
            <q>I don’t have time to cook, and diets never last for me.</q>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="jr rv">
          <span class="jr-h">
            Stage<small>and touchpoints</small>
          </span>
          <span class="jr-h">
            Feeling<small>low to high</small>
          </span>
          <span class="jr-h">Doing</span>
          <span class="jr-h">Thinking</span>
          <span class="jr-h">What nuru should do</span>
          <div class="jr-fe" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="vd jr-ax" style="left: calc(8% - 2px)"></span>
            <span class="vd jr-ax" style="left: calc(92% - 2px)"></span>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 100 600" preserveAspectRatio="none">
              <path d="M8,50 C8,100 39,100 39,150 C39,200 19.8,200 19.8,250 C19.8,300 70.2,300 70.2,350 C70.2,400 51.7,400 51.7,450 C51.7,500 92,500 92,550"></path>
            </svg>
            <span class="jr-d" style="left: 8%; top: 8.333%"></span>
            <span class="jr-fl" style="left: 0; top: 8.333%">
              tired, sceptical
            </span>
            <span class="jr-d" style="left: 39%; top: 25%"></span>
            <span class="jr-fl" style="left: 39%; top: 25%; transform: translateX(-50%)">
              curious
            </span>
            <span class="jr-d" style="left: 19.8%; top: 41.667%"></span>
            <span class="jr-fl" style="left: 0; top: 41.667%">
              hesitant
            </span>
            <span class="jr-d" style="left: 70.2%; top: 58.333%"></span>
            <span class="jr-fl" style="left: 70.2%; top: 58.333%; transform: translateX(-50%)">
              relieved
            </span>
            <span class="jr-d" style="left: 51.7%; top: 75%"></span>
            <span class="jr-fl" style="left: 51.7%; top: 75%; transform: translateX(-50%)">
              wobbly
            </span>
            <span class="jr-d" style="left: 92%; top: 91.667%"></span>
            <span class="jr-fl" style="right: 0; top: 91.667%">
              confident
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="jr-c jr-st">
            <b>Aware</b>
            <span>Social post, search, a friend’s referral</span>
            <em class="jr-fm">Feeling: tired, sceptical</em>
          </div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-do">Orders takeaway again after a late day. Sees a nuru post about work lunches.</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-th">“I don’t have time to cook, and diets never last for me.”</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-nu">Speak to busy lives, not to weight. Lead with free, practical tips.</div>

          <div class="jr-c jr-st">
            <b>Explore</b>
            <span>Home, Who it’s for, Tips and meal plans</span>
            <em class="jr-fm">Feeling: curious</em>
          </div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-do">Reads Why nuru, checks who it’s for and opens a sample meal plan.</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-th">“This looks doable. Are these real dietitians?”</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-nu">Show credentials and specialities early. Keep sample plans free.</div>

          <div class="jr-c jr-st">
            <b>Sign up and book</b>
            <span>Sign-up, intake, booking, payment</span>
            <em class="jr-fm">Feeling: hesitant</em>
          </div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-do">
            Creates an account, fills in the intake, picks a dietitian and a time, then pays.
          </div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-th">“That’s a lot of questions. I hope it’s worth it.”</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-nu">Keep the intake short and saved as he goes. Show the price before payment.</div>

          <div class="jr-c jr-st">
            <b>First consultation</b>
            <span>Video call, written plan, email summary</span>
            <em class="jr-fm">Feeling: relieved</em>
          </div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-do">Meets Elif on a video call. They agree on a goal and a first week.</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-th">“She asked about my week, not just my weight.”</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-nu">Send the plan the same day and invite him into the app.</div>

          <div class="jr-c jr-st">
            <b>Daily routine</b>
            <span>App: Home, My meals, reminders</span>
            <em class="jr-fm">Feeling: wobbly</em>
          </div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-do">Opens the app each morning, follows today’s menu, logs meals and water.</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-th">“I slipped on Wednesday. Have I ruined it?”</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-nu">Gentle reminders, no red marks. One tap to message the dietitian.</div>

          <div class="jr-c jr-st">
            <b>Follow-up and habit</b>
            <span>App: My dietitian, follow-up call</span>
            <em class="jr-fm">Feeling: confident</em>
          </div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-do">Reviews progress with Elif, adjusts the plan and cooks without checking it.</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-th">“It feels like my routine now, not a diet.”</div>
          <div class="jr-c jr-nu">Celebrate habits, not numbers. Offer lighter check-ins over time.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tb-p" role="tabpanel" hidden id="tp-sf" aria-labelledby="tb-sf">
        <div class="subh">
          <h3 class="h3">How a visitor moves from the public website to a booked consultation and into the app.</h3>
        </div>
        <div
          class="sf rv"
          role="group"
          aria-label="Site flow in three phases: discover on the public website, book a first consultation, then use the service with the dietitian and the app"
        >
          <div class="sf-row c5">
            <span class="sf-ph">Discover, on the public website</span>
            <span class="hd fr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk out" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Search, social or a referral</b>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk page" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Home</b>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk page" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Explore</b>
              <small>Why nuru · Who it’s for · Services · Dietitians · Tips and meal plans · Questions</small>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk dec" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Ready to talk to a dietitian?</b>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk page" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Free tips and meal plans</b>
              <small>comes back when ready</small>
            </div>
            <span class="sf-lb" style="left: 80%; top: -18px; transform: translateX(-50%)">
              not yet
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="sf-cx" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="vd fd" style="left: calc(70% - 2px); top: 8px; height: calc(50% - 8px)"></span>
            <span class="hd fl" style="left: 8.333%; right: 30%; top: calc(50% - 2px)"></span>
            <span class="vd fd" style="left: calc(8.333% - 2px); top: 50%; bottom: 6px"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-d" style="left: calc(8.333% - 4px); bottom: 0"></span>
            <span class="sf-lb" style="left: calc(70% + 12px)">
              yes
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="sf-row c6">
            <span class="sf-ph">Book a first consultation</span>
            <span class="hd fr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk clay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Create account</b>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk clay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Intake questionnaire</b>
              <small>routine, goals, health</small>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Dietitian match</b>
              <small>by speciality</small>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk clay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Choose a time</b>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk clay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Payment</b>
              <small>via payment provider</small>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk ink" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Booking confirmed</b>
              <small>email and reminder</small>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sf-cx" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="vd fd" style="left: calc(91.667% - 2px); top: 8px; height: calc(50% - 8px)"></span>
            <span class="hd fl" style="left: 10%; right: 8.333%; top: calc(50% - 2px)"></span>
            <span class="vd fd" style="left: calc(10% - 2px); top: 50%; bottom: 6px"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-d" style="left: calc(10% - 4px); bottom: 0"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="sf-row c5">
            <span class="sf-ph">Use, with the dietitian and the app</span>
            <span class="hd fr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk olive" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Video consultation</b>
              <small>client and dietitian</small>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk olive" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Personal plan</b>
              <small>written by the dietitian</small>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk clay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Download the app</b>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk clay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Client app</b>
              <small>Home · My meals · My dietitian · Profile</small>
            </div>
            <div class="sf-node">
              <span class="mk olive" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <b>Follow-up consultation</b>
              <small>progress review</small>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sf-cx" aria-hidden="true" style="height: 64px">
            <span class="vd fd" style="left: calc(90% - 2px); top: 8px; height: calc(50% - 8px)"></span>
            <span class="hd fl" style="left: 30%; right: 10%; top: calc(50% - 2px)"></span>
            <span class="vd fu" style="left: calc(30% - 2px); top: 14px; height: calc(50% - 14px)"></span>
            <span class="ah ah-u" style="left: calc(30% - 4px); top: 8px"></span>
            <span class="sf-lb" style="left: 60%; top: calc(50% + 8px); transform: translateX(-50%)">
              plan adjusted
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lg">
          <span>
            <span class="mk page"></span>Website page
          </span>
          <span>
            <span class="mk clay"></span>Client action
          </span>
          <span>
            <span class="mk ink"></span>nuru step
          </span>
          <span>
            <span class="mk olive"></span>With the dietitian
          </span>
          <span>
            <span class="mk out"></span>Outside nuru
          </span>
          <span>
            <span class="mk dec"></span>Decision
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tb-p" role="tabpanel" hidden id="tp-ar" aria-labelledby="tb-ar">
        <div class="subh">
          <h3 class="h3">The channels each group uses, the services behind them and the partners nuru relies on.</h3>
          <p class="tx" style="margin-top: 8px">
            Four channels, the website, the client app, a dietitian workspace and an admin CMS, share one API, eight
            services and four data stores.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="ar rv"
          role="group"
          aria-label="System architecture: clients, dietitians and the nuru team use four channels that share one API, eight services, four data stores and four external services"
        >
          <span class="al" style="grid-row: 1">
            People
